---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Presenter desk" description="Presenter run of show, preparation, prompts, and troubleshooting for Workshop 1.">
<div class="container">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Facilitator only · use alongside the deck</div><h1>Presenter desk</h1><p>Keep the session moving with a visible run of show, setup checks, recovery guidance, and ready-to-copy Copilot prompts.</p></section>
  <section class="grid two">
    <article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Session timer</div><h2 id="timer">180:00</h2><p class="muted">A simple pacing aid. Start it when the workshop begins.</p><div class="actions"><button class="btn primary" id="timer-start">Start</button><button class="btn" id="timer-pause">Pause</button><button class="btn" id="timer-reset">Reset</button></div></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">North star</div><h2>Working site, not perfect site.</h2><p>By the end, every student should own a repository, have made a reviewable change, and have a live URL or a documented recovery path.</p><a class="btn" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL+'slides/'}>Launch slides ↗</a></article>
  </section>
  <section class="section presenter-grid">
    <nav class="side-nav" aria-label="Presenter sections"><a href="#prep">Before the session</a><a href="#runofshow">Run of show</a><a href="#prompts">Copilot prompt bank</a><a href="#recovery">Catch-up plan</a><a href="#troubleshoot">Troubleshooting</a><a href="#exit">Exit check</a></nav>
    <div class="content-stack">
      <article class="card" id="prep"><h2>Before the session</h2><div class="checklist">
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Test the workshop URL and presenter slides on the classroom network.</span></label>
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Verify the starter repo is public or students have access.</span></label>
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Test GitHub Pages deployment from a fresh clone.</span></label>
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Confirm students can access Copilot via their student licenses.</span></label>
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Prepare repository-ready and site-ready checkpoint copies.</span></label>
        <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/><span>Have a fallback path for missing installs or account access.</span></label>
      </div></article>
      <article class="card" id="runofshow"><h2>Run of show · teaching notes</h2>
        <h3>0:00–0:25 · orient and unblock</h3><p>Show a finished portfolio first. Keep environment setup time-boxed: if a student is blocked after the setup segment, pair them with a working machine or checkpoint so learning can continue.</p>
        <h3>0:25–1:05 · repository and VS Code</h3><p>Explain Git vs GitHub with a diagram. Let students choose one layout, create their own repository, and find the Source Control panel. Avoid deep Git internals.</p>
        <h3>1:05–1:35 · personalize and preview</h3><p>Demonstrate a short Copilot request, then inspect the diff. Ask students to add resume sections and preview the site locally. Remind them that public pages expose whatever they publish.</p>
        <h3>1:45–2:15 · requirement through pull request</h3><p>Have each student create one issue with acceptance criteria. Their implementation should be small enough to review. Require them to explain the diff before merging.</p>
        <h3>2:15–2:45 · deploy and validate</h3><p>Show where the Pages deployment workflow runs. Explain that a successful local preview doesn't prove the deployed path works. Check Actions logs and the actual published URL.</p>
        <h3>2:45–3:00 · recovery and close</h3><p>Protect the final 15 minutes. Students who are behind use checkpoints; those finished polish accessibility or content. Capture live URLs and one takeaway.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="prompts"><h2>Copilot prompt bank</h2>
        <div class="prompt"><h3>Explain before editing</h3><pre>Explain the files, how this Astro project renders the page, and where content and styling are defined. Don't edit files yet. Give me a short map of the project.</pre><button class="btn small copy-prompt">Copy prompt</button></div>
        <div class="prompt"><h3>Implement a focused requirement</h3><pre>Requirement: add a featured project card titled [PROJECT]. Acceptance criteria: title, short summary, relevant skills, and a working link; responsive on mobile; no new dependencies. Propose a plan before editing, then show me the changed files.</pre><button class="btn small copy-prompt">Copy prompt</button></div>
        <div class="prompt"><h3>Review generated changes</h3><pre>Review the diff against these acceptance criteria: [CRITERIA]. Look for broken links, accessibility issues, responsive layout regressions, hard-coded secrets, and unnecessary complexity. Report findings before changing anything.</pre><button class="btn small copy-prompt">Copy prompt</button></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="recovery"><h2>Late-arrival and catch-up protocol</h2>
        <ol><li>Ask what already works; do not restart the entire setup.</li><li>Give the student the current checkpoint repository or completed example.</li><li>Have them create their own repository and personalize at least one item.</li><li>Rejoin the shared exercise at the next milestone.</li><li>Record what they skipped and share the page for self-paced review.</li></ol>
        <div class="notice">For a student arriving halfway through, prioritize the repository, one reviewed change, and deployment. Use pre-built checkpoints to preserve the learning objectives without requiring every earlier step.</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="troubleshoot"><h2>Troubleshooting quick guide</h2>
        <h3>GitHub sign-in fails</h3><p>Verify browser sign-in and VS Code authentication separately. Check that the student is using the intended GitHub account and has access to the repository.</p>
        <h3>Copilot isn't available</h3><p>Check the account shown in VS Code, license activation, and the Copilot extension status. Have the student follow the exercise instructions without AI while the access issue is resolved.</p>
        <h3>Local site runs but Pages is broken</h3><p>Inspect the latest Actions run, check the configured Pages source, and confirm the site's base path matches the repository name.</p>
        <h3>Student gets a merge conflict</h3><p>Have them pause and read the conflict markers. Explain the two competing versions before accepting either one; use the checkpoint branch if time is short.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card" id="exit"><h2>Exit check</h2><ul><li>Repository URL works and contains the student's project.</li><li>At least one issue / branch / pull request flow was completed or demonstrated with a checkpoint.</li><li>Live site URL is recorded, or the exact deployment blocker is known.</li><li>Student can state one Git concept and one Copilot change they reviewed.</li></ul><p class="muted small">Keep public portfolio content professional. Students should not publish private contact details, credentials, or information about other people without permission.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<script>
let remaining=180*60, interval=null;const el=document.querySelector('#timer');function draw(){el.textContent=String(Math.floor(remaining/60)).padStart(2,'0')+':'+String(remaining%60).padStart(2,'0')}document.querySelector('#timer-start').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(interval)return;interval=setInterval(()=>{if(remaining>0){remaining--;draw()}else{clearInterval(interval);interval=null}},1000)});document.querySelector('#timer-pause').addEventListener('click',()=>{clearInterval(interval);interval=null});document.querySelector('#timer-reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{clearInterval(interval);interval=null;remaining=10800;draw()});draw();
document.querySelectorAll('.copy-prompt').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',async()=>{try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(b.parentElement.querySelector('pre').textContent);b.textContent='Copied ✓'}catch{b.textContent='Select and copy'}setTimeout(()=>b.textContent='Copy prompt',1400)}));
</script>
</BaseLayout>